.TH XD\-WIFI\-KEY 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-wifi\-key \- ask for a wireless network's key
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-wifi\-key
.I ssid
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-wifi\-key
is an internal helper of XeonDesktop: the network icon of
.BR xd\-shell (1)
and the New Connection Wizard of
.BR xd\-netconn (1)
run it to ask for the key of a secured wireless network, in Windows XP's
Wireless Network Connection box (the key typed twice).
It prints the key on standard output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when a key was entered, 1 when the box was cancelled, 2 for wrong
arguments.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xd\-shell (1),
.BR xd\-netconn (1)
